File: SchurRings.info, Node: jacobiTrudi, Next: jacobiTrudi_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmMemoize=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, Prev: internalProduct_lpRingElement_cmRingElement_rp, Up: Top

jacobiTrudi -- Jacobi-Trudi determinant
***************************************

  * Usage: 
        f = jacobiTrudi(lambda,R)
  * Inputs:
      * lambda, a *note basic list: (Macaulay2Doc)BasicList,, a nonincreasing
        list of integers, or a partition
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, a Symmetric ring
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note EorH: EorH, => ..., default value "E", e- or h- representation of
        Jacobi-Trudi determinant
      * *note Memoize: jacobiTrudi_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmMemoize=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value true, Store values of the jacobiTrudi function.
  * Outputs:
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, an element of a
        Symmetric ring

Description
===========



Given a partition lambda and Symmetric ring R, the method evaluates the
Jacobi-Trudi determinant corresponding to the partition lambda, yielding a
representation of the Schur function s_{lambda} as a symmetric function in R.
The default option is to represent this symmetric function in terms of
e-polynomials.



+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = symmetricRing(QQ,10);                            |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : jacobiTrudi({3,2,2,1},R)                             |
|                                                          |
|               2                                          |
|o2 = e e e  - e  - e e e  + e e                           |
|      1 3 4    4    1 2 5    2 6                          |
|                                                          |
|o2 : R                                                    |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : jacobiTrudi(new Partition from {4,4,1},R,EorH => "H")|
|                                                          |
|        2                                                 |
|o3 = h h  - h h h  - h h  + h h                           |
|      1 4    1 3 5    4 5    3 6                          |
|                                                          |
|o3 : R                                                    |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : toS oo                                               |
|                                                          |
|o4 = s                                                    |
|      4,4,1                                               |
|                                                          |
|o4 : schurRing (QQ, s, 10)                                |
+----------------------------------------------------------+



Selecting EorH => "H" uses the conjugate determinant formula $s_\lambda =
\det(h_{\lambda_i - i + j})$.  The two branches produce different e- vs
h-polynomials but always represent the same Schur function:



+-----------------------------------------+
|i5 : R = symmetricRing(QQ,8);            |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i6 : lam = {4,3,2,1};                    |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i7 : fe = jacobiTrudi(lam,R,EorH => "E");|
+-----------------------------------------+
|i8 : fh = jacobiTrudi(lam,R,EorH => "H");|
+-----------------------------------------+
|i9 : toS fe                              |
|                                         |
|o9 = s                                   |
|      4,3,2,1                            |
|                                         |
|o9 : schurRing (QQ, s, 8)                |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i10 : toS fh                             |
|                                         |
|o10 = s                                  |
|       4,3,2,1                           |
|                                         |
|o10 : schurRing (QQ, s, 8)               |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i11 : toS fe == toS fh                   |
|                                         |
|o11 = true                               |
+-----------------------------------------+



The routine caches intermediate subdeterminants on the ring via *note
jacobiTrudi(...,Memoize=>...):
jacobiTrudi_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmMemoize=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,, so a second call on a large
partition returns almost instantly:



+-------------------------------------------+
|i12 : R = symmetricRing(QQ,6);             |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i13 : elapsedTime jacobiTrudi({4,3,2,1},R);|
| -- .00046938s elapsed                     |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i14 : elapsedTime jacobiTrudi({4,3,2,1},R);|
| -- .000019055s elapsed                    |
+-------------------------------------------+



Passing a partition through *note toSymm: toSymm, applied to the corresponding
Schur label reproduces the Jacobi-Trudi output:



+-------------------------------------------------+
|i15 : R = symmetricRing(QQ,5);                   |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i16 : S = schurRing R;                           |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i17 : jacobiTrudi({3,2,1},R) == toSymm(S_{3,2,1})|
|                                                 |
|o17 = true                                       |
+-------------------------------------------------+



jacobiTrudi works over tensor products of Symmetric rings, producing a
determinant in the outermost set of generators:



+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i18 : R = symmetricRing(QQ, 4, EHPVariables => (a,b,c));|
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i19 : T = symmetricRing(R, 3, EHPVariables => (x,y,z)); |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i20 : jacobiTrudi({2,1},T)                              |
|                                                        |
|o20 = x x  - x                                          |
|       1 2    3                                         |
|                                                        |
|o20 : T                                                 |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i21 : jacobiTrudi({3,2},T, EorH => "H")                 |
|                                                        |
|o21 = y y                                               |
|       2 3                                              |
|                                                        |
|o21 : T                                                 |
+--------------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use jacobiTrudi:
========================

  * "jacobiTrudi(BasicList,Ring)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note jacobiTrudi: jacobiTrudi, is a *note method function with
options: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in SchurRings.m2:6102:0.

File: SchurRings.info, Node: jacobiTrudi_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmMemoize=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, Next: kostkaNumber, Prev: jacobiTrudi, Up: Top

jacobiTrudi(...,Memoize=>...) -- Store values of the jacobiTrudi function.
**************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        Memoize => b
  * Inputs:
      * b, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========



If the option is set to true then all the values of the jacobiTrudi function
that are computed are recorded into a special hash table attached to the
symmetric ring inside which the computations are done.  This makes repeated
evaluations on related partitions substantially faster, at the cost of some
extra memory in the ring.



+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = symmetricRing(QQ,6);                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : jacobiTrudi({4,3,2,1},R,Memoize => true) ==                             |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = true                                                                    |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|jacobiTrudi({4,3,2,1},R,Memoize => false)                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
