plethysm(RingElement,ClassFunction) -- Plethystic operations on class functions
*******************************************************************************

  * Function: *note plethysm: plethysm,
  * Usage: 
        pl = plethysm(f,cF)
        pl = plethysm(lambda,cF)
  * Inputs:
      * a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,
      * a *note Class function: ClassFunction,

Description
===========



These methods describe the result of applying plethystic operations to a
virtual character of a symmetric group. These operations are described either
via a symmetric function f, or a partition lambda. Since cF corresponds to an
S_n- representation, the option *note GroupActing: GroupActing, is irrelevant
in this case.



+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : cF = new ClassFunction from {{2} => 1, {1,1} => -1};|
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : pl1 = plethysm({1,1},cF)                            |
|                                                         |
|o2 = ClassFunction{{1, 1} => 1}                          |
|                   {2} => 1                              |
|                                                         |
|o2 : ClassFunction                                       |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : R = symmetricRing 5;                                |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : pl2 = plethysm(e_1+e_2,cF)                          |
|                                                         |
|o4 = ClassFunction{{1, 1} => 0}                          |
|                   {2} => 2                              |
|                                                         |
|o4 : ClassFunction                                       |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : S = schurRing R;                                    |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : symmetricFunction(cF,S)                             |
|                                                         |
|o6 = -s                                                  |
|       1,1                                               |
|                                                         |
|o6 : S                                                   |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : symmetricFunction(pl1,S)                            |
|                                                         |
|o7 = s                                                   |
|      2                                                  |
|                                                         |
|o7 : S                                                   |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : symmetricFunction(pl2,S)                            |
|                                                         |
|o8 = s  - s                                              |
|      2    1,1                                           |
|                                                         |
|o8 : S                                                   |
+---------------------------------------------------------+



Applying the partition \{2\} to the sign character of S_2 gives Sym^2 of the
sign, which is the trivial representation of S_4:



+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : sgn = new ClassFunction from {{2} => -1, {1,1} => 1};           |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : pl = plethysm({2},sgn)                                         |
|                                                                     |
|o10 = ClassFunction{{1, 1} => 1}                                     |
|                    {2} => 1                                         |
|                                                                     |
|o10 : ClassFunction                                                  |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : symmetricFunction(pl, schurRing(QQ, s, 4, GroupActing => "Sn"))|
|                                                                     |
|o11 = s                                                              |
|       2                                                             |
|                                                                     |
|o11 : schurRing (QQ, s, 4)                                           |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+



Plethysm by a power-sum class function is Adams-type: p_k sends a
representation to its k-th Adams operation (on class functions).



+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : cF2 = new ClassFunction from {{3} => 2, {2,1} => 0, {1,1,1} => -1};|
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : R2 = symmetricRing 4;                                              |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : plethysm(p_2, cF2)                                                 |
|                                                                         |
|o14 = ClassFunction{{1, 1, 1} => -1}                                     |
|                    {2, 1} => -1                                         |
|                    {3} => 2                                             |
|                                                                         |
|o14 : ClassFunction                                                      |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * "plethysm(BasicList,ClassFunction)"
  * *note plethysm(RingElement,ClassFunction):
    plethysm_lpRingElement_cmClassFunction_rp, -- Plethystic operations on
    class functions
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

