schurLevel -- Number of SchurRings the ring is a tensor product of.
*******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        lev = schurLevel(R)
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, 
  * Outputs:
      * lev, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 

Description
===========



For the representation ring R of a product of lev general linear and/or
symmetric groups, the function returns lev.  If R is not a representation ring,
the function returns 0.



+---------------------------+
|i1 : R = schurRing(QQ,r,3);|
+---------------------------+
|i2 : S = schurRing(R,s,5); |
+---------------------------+
|i3 : T = schurRing(S,t,2); |
+---------------------------+
|i4 : schurLevel R          |
|                           |
|o4 = 1                     |
+---------------------------+
|i5 : schurLevel S          |
|                           |
|o5 = 2                     |
+---------------------------+
|i6 : schurLevel T          |
|                           |
|o6 = 3                     |
+---------------------------+
|i7 : schurLevel QQ         |
|                           |
|o7 = 0                     |
+---------------------------+



A three-level tower mixing GL-factors with an S_n-factor counts each layer,
regardless of which group is acting:



+-----------------------------------------------+
|i8 : A = schurRing(QQ,a,3);                    |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i9 : B = schurRing(A,b,4);                     |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i10 : C = schurRing(B,c,2,GroupActing => "Sn");|
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i11 : schurLevel C                             |
|                                               |
|o11 = 3                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------+



A Symmetric ring (produced by *note symmetricRing: symmetricRing,) sits over a
single tower slot and reports schurLevel equal to 1, while an ordinary
polynomial ring or the base field report 0:



+-------------------------------------+
|i12 : schurLevel(symmetricRing(QQ,5))|
|                                     |
|o12 = 1                              |
+-------------------------------------+
|i13 : schurLevel(QQ[x,y,z])          |
|                                     |
|o13 = 0                              |
+-------------------------------------+
|i14 : schurLevel ZZ                  |
|                                     |
|o14 = 0                              |
+-------------------------------------+

Ways to use schurLevel:
=======================

  * "schurLevel(Ring)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note schurLevel: schurLevel, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

